# ATLAS CONTROL FLOW GRAPH (CFG)
## Target Profile: CONTRACT-QEMU-VIRT-AARCH64-M1 (Cryptographic SHA-256 + Disjoint Stack)
*Formerly designated Alpha in early bootstrap drafting.*

```text
[Entry: 0x00000000 (_start)]
  │
  ├─> Mask DAIF interrupts (msr daifset, #0xf)
  ├─> Set SP = 0x401FC000 (Scratchpad stack, disjoint from descriptor by 8 KiB gap)
  ├─> Set UART Base = 0x09000000 (x20)
  ├─> Call print_string(msg_awaken) ──> [print_string] ──> [Return]
  ├─> Populate Boot Descriptor at 0x401FE000 (x22)
  ├─> Call print_string(msg_verify) ──> [print_string] ──> [Return]
  │
  ▼
[Cryptographic Verification: sha256_256bytes]
  │
  ├─> Arg 0: x0 = 0x40200000 (Physics payload base)
  ├─> Arg 1: x1 = 0x401FE100 (Padding & block scratch buffer)
  ├─> Arg 2: x2 = 0x401FE080 (32-byte digest output buffer)
  ├─> bl sha256_256bytes (NIST FIPS 180-4 pure AArch64 software implementation)
  │
  ▼
[Compare Digest: 32-Byte Constant-Time Check]
  │
  ├─> Compare 8 x 32-bit words against pinned digest (e1d89bb1...374c)
  │
  ├── [ANY MISMATCH: b.ne] ─────────────────┐
  │                                         │
  ▼ [EXACT MATCH]                           ▼ [.Lrefuse_handoff]
[Emit Handoff Checkpoint]                   │
  │                                         ├─> Call print_string(msg_refuse)
  ├─> Call print_string(msg_handoff)        │
  │                                         ▼
  ▼                                       [.Lquiescent_halt] <──────┐
[Setup PHYSICS_ENTRY_ABI]                   │                       │
  │                                         ├─> wfe                 │ (Quiescent halt)
  ├─> mov x0, 0x401FE000 (Descriptor)       └─> b .Lquiescent_halt ─┘
  ├─> mov x1, 256 (Payload size)
  ├─> ldr x2, =0x5048595349435330 ('PHYSICS0' cookie)
  ├─> ldr x19, =0x40200000 (Static Target Proof: literal loaded directly into x19)
  │
  ▼
[Handoff to Physics]
  │
  ├─> br x19 (Branch to target-proven address 0x40200000)
  │
  ▼ [UNREACHABLE FALLTHROUGH TRAP]
  └─> b .Lquiescent_halt

[Subroutine: print_string]
  │
  ├─> .Lprint_char: ldrb w0, [x21], #1
  ├─> cbz w0, .Lprint_ret
  ├─> str w0, [x20] (UART MMIO Polled Write)
  ├─> b .Lprint_char
  └─> .Lprint_ret: ret
```
